  "title": "Weaver became a public multimodal agent",
  "summary": "Pollinations grew a public multimodal agent while making the models, media tools, and fallback routes behind it more capable and resilient.\n\nPolli-agent arrived as an OpenAI-compatible streaming endpoint that coordinates text, images, audio, video, web search, and media tools. It was then named Weaver, added to the model catalog, and made callable as `voodoohop/weaver`. Approved community agents also gained short-lived delegated tokens, so they can generate within a caller’s existing Pollen controls without handling the caller’s API key.\n\nCommunity model owners can nominate compatible public backups. A shared fallback executor extended that approach across text, images, video, audio, embeddings, and 3D, with routing records showing which model served a request. Image capacity improved too: FLUX.1 Schnell gained a backup route, Z-Image workers now pass a health check before joining capacity, and DreamShaper’s parallel GPU pipelines raised measured concurrent throughput from about 4.3 to 8 images per second per card.\n\nElevenLabs gained multi-speaker dialogue, voice isolation from uploaded media, and character-aligned TTS timestamps. Transcription moved to AssemblyAI Universal-3.5 Pro at the same base rate, while Kokoro added 54 voices and five output formats to the existing speech endpoints. That covers more of the path from raw recording to captioned, generated speech.\n\nGPT Realtime 2.1 Mini, Nemotron 3 Ultra, Mistral OCR 4, Cohere Command A+, Qwen3.7 Flash, and Inkling Small joined existing routes for realtime sessions, long-context chat, document extraction, and multimodal work. DeepSeek moved to its V4 Flash 0731 checkpoint; several other models changed providers while keeping their public interfaces.",
  "pr_count": 73,
